# Configuration

*Reference.* What this pack's config file holds, and what belongs to core instead.

## The file and its key

`config/{{bladeNamespace}}.php`, merged at `ichava.{{bladeNamespace}}`. **The filename must
match the package short name** -- a different name silently doubles the key and every read returns
`null`, which shipped undetected in this ecosystem once before.

```bash
php artisan vendor:publish --tag=ichava::{{bladeNamespace}}-config
```

Publishing is optional; the defaults are merged either way.

## What is here

Only what is specific to this pack -- the set name and prefix it registers under, and its own
addressing defaults. Read the published file for the current list rather than a copy of it here.

## Kinds in `config.json`

`resources/assets/svg/config.json` declares what the pack's SVGs are, `icon` or `illustration`. Core decides
each item's kind from the first row that gives one, and an item path is the file's path under `files/` without
`.svg` (`illustrations/office`):

| Row | Key | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | the host's `kinds.overrides` | the app developer's, in core's config; wins over the pack |
| 2 | `metadata.data.items.<item path>.kind` | one item; the value is an object so it can grow |
| 3 | `metadata.data.kinds.rules[]` | `{ "match": "<glob>", "kind": "..." }`, ordered, **first match wins**; put specific rules before broad ones |
| 4 | `metadata.data.categories.<slug>.kind` | every item in that first-level folder |
| 5 | `package.kind` | this pack's default, `{{kind}}` |
| 6 | | `icon` |

Globs match the whole item path and are case-sensitive: `*` is any run of characters except `/`, `?` is one
character, and `**` is whole segments (`spot/**`). `items` and `kinds.rules` start empty. A pack is "mixed" when
its items resolve to both kinds; nothing declares that, and there is no `"kind": "mixed"`. A value that names no
kind is ignored by core and reported by `ichava::ichava-core.info doctor`; the pack's own `ResourceShapeTest`
fails on it instead. See core's [kinds guide](https://github.com/ichava/core/blob/main/docs/kinds.md).

## What is not here

Cache, queue, database, logging, security and the `ICHAVA_*` environment surface are **core's**, and
apply to every pack at once. See core's [configuration guide](https://github.com/ichava/core/blob/main/docs/configuration.md) and
[environment variables](https://github.com/ichava/core/blob/main/docs/environment.md).

A value set here cannot change how core seeds, caches or sanitises; that is the point of the split.

